{% doc %}
  BMP size guide — the modal dialog holding the size chart, and the home of the
  feature's own presentation settings (link text, icon) and of every chart, as
  child blocks. The global "BMP: Size guide" panel is retired.

  The option name is NOT one of them, deliberately. It identifies the store's
  size axis for the server-side add-to-cart gate, which runs from
  blocks/buy-buttons.liquid and blocks/accelerated-checkout.liquid on every
  product template — including templates with no size-guide block at all, which
  must keep working. Liquid gives those blocks no
  way to read this one's settings, so the name stays a theme setting
  (`settings.bmp_size_guide_option`, "BMP: Size" panel) and exactly one naming
  setting serves both features by design. It is read below, not declared.

  The visible trigger is NOT here: it renders inside the variant picker's
  option legend (`Size: M … Size Guide`) via snippets/bmp-size-guide-trigger,
  called from the contracted edit in snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid —
  the original design's in-row placement. Because the name is a theme setting,
  that snippet gates itself SERVER-SIDE on the legend's option name, exactly as
  it always has: one trigger per product, in the right legend, in
  the first response. The two presentation values it cannot read from here leave
  this block by two different routes: the LABEL is published as
  data-bmp-size-guide-label on the dialog-component and copied onto the trigger
  by assets/bmp-size-guide-portal.js, while the ICON never crosses into JS at
  all — the per-product `style` tag below either emits its rule or does not.
  The dialog renders only when the product has a matching option.

  There is deliberately no `data-bmp-size-guide-icon` attribute. It existed only
  to be read by a `:has()` rule in the trigger's static sheet, which is the
  document-wide shape this follow-up replaced; publishing it now would be a
  second, unread source of truth for a value the `style` tag already decides.

  In the theme editor only (request.design_mode), a product WITHOUT that option
  renders a visible placeholder instead. It carries block.shopify_attributes so
  selecting the block in the sidebar still scrolls to and outlines something —
  a `hidden` element has no box and no rect, so it is a dead editor target, and
  this is precisely when the merchant is looking for an explanation. Zero bytes
  on the live storefront.

  The dialog-component's id is per-product
  (`id="bmp-size-guide-dialog-{{ closest.product.id }}"`), because quick-add
  clones the whole product page into its popup (assets/quick-add.js), and a
  fixed id would leave the host product's dialog and the quick-added
  product's dialog sharing one id on the same page. The trigger carries the same
  product id as a data attribute and assets/bmp-size-guide-portal.js rebuilds the
  dialog id from it — not an `on:click` `#id` binding, which Horizon resolves
  with document.querySelector, i.e. first match in document order.

  The dialog also carries a bare `data-bmp-size-guide-dialog` attribute, which
  is how assets/bmp-size-guide-portal.js finds size-guide dialogs generically
  (parsing a fetched page, spotting a quick-add clone) without knowing whose
  product they belong to.

  The trigger's REVEAL is emitted from here, per product, by the Liquid `style`
  tag inside the dialog-component. That placement is the whole mechanism and
  each half of it is load-bearing:

    - a `style` tag rather than the `stylesheet` block below, because
      only the former renders Liquid, and the rule has to carry a product id:
      `.bmp-size-guide__trigger[data-bmp-size-guide-product="…"]`. A static
      sheet can only say "this document holds SOME size-guide dialog", and a
      document can hold a second product's variant picker
      (sections/featured-product{,-information}.liquid render one for a
      merchant-chosen product) or a quick-add's adopted dialog. Under the old
      document-wide guard those pages revealed a trigger whose click resolves
      nothing, and showed the icon on a product whose own toggle is off.
    - INSIDE the dialog-component rather than beside it, because the rule has
      to travel with the node. On mobile quick-add, updateQuickAddModal drops
      `.product-details` (assets/quick-add.js) and the portal re-fetches the
      product page and adopts the `[data-bmp-size-guide-dialog]` element alone
      — a sibling `<style>` would be left behind in the parse document and the
      trigger in the popup would never come back.

  So the reveal ships exactly where the dialog ships, on the server, in the
  first response, with no JS between the response and a visible trigger. This
  is the one place in the feature where Liquid is allowed to interpolate CSS
  (the layer's second sanctioned exception).

  The modal content is composed of child blocks; the private
  _bmp-size-guide-image child shows its image only when its "Product type"
  setting matches the current product's type, so one template serves every
  product type with a per-type chart. A child with an EMPTY "Product type" is
  the default chart: it renders whenever no typed child matched,
  and the stylesheet below hides it the moment one did — before, an unmatched
  product opened an empty dialog.

  Replaces the old window-global modal (inline script, duplicate-id
  workarounds) with Horizon's stock dialog-component (focus trap, ESC,
  scroll-lock).
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign bmp_sg_option_name = settings.bmp_size_guide_option | strip | default: 'Size'

  # Nil-safe, the same rule scripts/check-size-required.mjs enforces for
  # bmp_size_required in this feature: an unmaterialised setting reads as nil,
  # the schema default is true, so nil must mean ON. templates/product.json
  # ships this block instance with `"settings": {}` — a bare truthiness test
  # would render the icon OFF on the theme's own product template until a
  # merchant re-saved the block, contradicting the default it declares.
  assign bmp_sg_icon = true
  if block.settings.bmp_size_guide_icon == false
    assign bmp_sg_icon = false
  endif
  # Same reason, and it is an accessible name: an unmaterialised text setting
  # would leave the dialog with aria-label="".
  assign bmp_sg_default_label = 'bmp.content.bmp_size_guide_default_label' | t
  assign bmp_sg_label = block.settings.bmp_size_guide_label | strip_html | strip | default: bmp_sg_default_label
  assign bmp_sg_has_size = false
  for option in closest.product.options
    if option == bmp_sg_option_name
      assign bmp_sg_has_size = true
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if bmp_sg_has_size -%}
  <script
    src="{{ 'dialog.js' | asset_url }}"
    type="module"
    fetchpriority="low"
  ></script>

  <dialog-component
    id="bmp-size-guide-dialog-{{ closest.product.id }}"
    data-bmp-size-guide-dialog
    data-bmp-size-guide-config
    data-bmp-size-guide-label="{{ bmp_sg_label | escape }}"
    class="bmp-size-guide"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      The trigger's reveal, and the icon's, keyed on THIS product's id. See the
      header: a `style` tag because it renders Liquid, and inside this element
      because the portal adopts this element alone on the mobile quick-add
      route. Only `display` is interpolated — every other trigger declaration
      stays in the static, cacheable sheet in
      snippets/bmp-size-guide-trigger.liquid, where it is harmless while the
      button is still `display: none`.

      The icon arm is conditional rather than value-interpolated: the setting
      decides whether the rule EXISTS, so a store with the icon off ships two
      fewer lines instead of a second `display: none`.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% style %}
      .bmp-size-guide__trigger[data-bmp-size-guide-product="{{ closest.product.id }}"] {
        display: inline-flex;
      }

      {% if bmp_sg_icon %}
        .bmp-size-guide__trigger[data-bmp-size-guide-product="{{ closest.product.id }}"]
          .bmp-size-guide__trigger-icon {
          display: inline-flex;
        }
      {% endif %}
    {% endstyle %}

    <dialog
      ref="dialog"
      class="bmp-size-guide__dialog dialog-modal"
      on:click="/closeDialogOnClickOutside"
      on:keydown="/closeDialogOnEscapePress"
      scroll-lock
      aria-label="{{ bmp_sg_label | escape }}"
    >
      <button
        type="button"
        class="button close-button bmp-size-guide__close button-unstyled"
        on:click="dialog-component/closeDialog"
        aria-label="{{ 'actions.close_dialog' | t }}"
      >
        <span class="svg-wrapper">
          {{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>
      </button>

      <div class="bmp-size-guide__content">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </dialog>
  </dialog-component>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Visible on purpose, and deliberately WITHOUT data-bmp-size-guide-config.
    The missing-block warning only renders on a legend whose option matches the
    configured name, so a product that has no such option produces no warning
    for this to suppress — emitting the marker here would only risk hiding a
    warning somewhere else on the page (a design-mode quick-add clone).

    The chart children are NOT rendered here, and that is a platform limit, not
    a preference: Shopify rejects a block file that contains more than one
    `content_for 'blocks'`, even across mutually exclusive branches — the upload
    fails with "Duplicate entries for 'content_for "blocks"'". `shopify theme
    check` does not catch it; only the upload does. So on a product without the
    configured option every chart child stays a dead editor target: selecting
    one in the sidebar scrolls to nothing. That is pre-existing — the original
    version of this block had the same gap behind a hidden span — and closing it needs
    a different shape (one `content_for` reached by both paths, or a separate
    snippet), which is tracked separately rather than smuggled in here.

    What this branch does fix is the PARENT: a `hidden` element has no box and
    no rect, so selecting the block itself used to scroll to nothing, precisely
    when the merchant is looking for the explanation.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="bmp-size-guide__editor-note" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {{- 'bmp.content.bmp_size_guide_block_no_option' | t: option: bmp_sg_option_name -}}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* ONE geometry at every viewport (old-theme reference): a top-anchored
     box that hugs its content and scrolls internally. height: fit-content
     (not auto — fixed-position dialogs stretch on auto) also neutralizes
     the native .dialog-modal mobile rule that turns dialogs into 100dvh
     sheets, so nothing jumps at the 750px breakpoint. The top gap comes
     from inset, not margin: the native open animation animates margin-top
     to 0 with fill forwards, which permanently overrides author margins. */
  .bmp-size-guide__dialog {
    width: min(42rem, calc(100% - var(--margin-lg) * 2));
    height: fit-content;
    max-height: calc(100dvh - var(--margin-lg) * 2);
    inset-block-start: var(--margin-lg);
    inset-block-end: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--padding-xl);
    overflow-y: auto;
    border: none;
    border-radius: var(--style-border-radius-popover);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }

  .bmp-size-guide__close {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--padding-sm);
    inset-inline-end: var(--padding-sm);
  }

  /* The 44px button reserves a good touch target but the stock icon draws
     at 14px and reads too small in this large dialog. Scoped to this
     dialog's close button only. */
  .bmp-size-guide__close .svg-wrapper,
  .bmp-size-guide__close svg {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
  }

  .bmp-size-guide__content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-md);
    padding-block-start: var(--padding-lg);
  }

  .bmp-size-guide__content img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Default-chart fallback: a chart child with an empty "Product
     type" renders as the default and is suppressed the moment any typed
     child matched the product — a typed chart always wins. Sibling
     comparison is impossible in Liquid (blocks render in isolation), so the
     "no other child matches" condition lives here, on the classes the
     children emit. */
  .bmp-size-guide__content:has(.bmp-size-guide__image--match) .bmp-size-guide__image--default {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Two blank-type children would both claim the default slot; only the
     first one renders. */
  .bmp-size-guide__image--default ~ .bmp-size-guide__image--default {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Theme-editor placeholder for a product with no option matching the
     configured size axis. Never rendered on the live storefront. */
  .bmp-size-guide__editor-note {
    padding: var(--padding-sm);
    border: 1px dashed rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 30%);
    border-radius: var(--style-border-radius-popover);
    font-size: var(--font-size--sm);
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:bmp.names.bmp_size_guide",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_bmp-size-guide-image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "type": "group"
    },
    {
      "type": "image"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:bmp.content.bmp_size_guide_block_help"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "bmp_size_guide_label",
      "label": "t:settings.text",
      "default": "t:bmp.text_defaults.bmp_size_guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "bmp_size_guide_icon",
      "label": "t:settings.icon",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:bmp.names.bmp_size_guide"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
